-- title:
--   Toric line in the eigenplane with Frobenius scalar a_q(g) q
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform such that for no proper divisor $M'$ of $M$ is there a normalised eigenform of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $q$-expansion coefficients at the primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q\mid M$ prime, $q\notin S$), with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$, for all such $\ell$. Let $\mathcal{O}''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a characteristic-zero field that is an $\mathcal{O}''$-algebra, and $\varphi:\mathrm{range}\,\chi_g\to K$ a ring homomorphism. Write $T$ for the $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Nat.Primes}\ \mathbb{Z}$-submodule of sequences $x:\mathbb{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$, where $J_0(M)$ is the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with its Hecke action [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82). Assume given a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ whose scalar action is computed level by level through the reductions $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda\to\mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$; a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (as automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$) to $\mathcal{O}''$-endomorphisms of $\mathcal{O}''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T$ satisfying $\rho_M(\sigma)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes y$ whenever $y=\sigma\cdot x$ componentwise; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from the Hecke polynomial ring to the same endomorphism ring with $T_M(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$; and a $K$-subspace $W$ of $K\otimes_{\mathcal{O}''}(\mathcal{O}''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of dimension $2$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M(\sigma)$, on which the base change of $T_M(\mathrm{heckeGen}\,\ell)$ acts as the scalar $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Then for every prime $q\neq\lambda$ with $q\mid M$ and $q^2\nmid M$, and every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit, there are a $K$-subspace $L\leq W$ with $\dim_K L=1$ and an integer $a\in\{1,-1\}$ with $a_q(g)=a$ in $\mathbb{C}$ such that every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting as $x\mapsto x^q$ on the residue field of $A$ satisfies $\rho_M(\sigma)w=(a\,q)\,w$ for all $w\in L$ and $\rho_M(\sigma)w-a\,w\in L$ for all $w\in W$ (after base change to $K$).
--
--   This is the local description at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level of the two-dimensional Hecke eigenplane attached to a weight-two newform inside the $\lambda$-adic Tate module of $J_0(M)$: the Frobenius-stable line coming from the toric part of the reduction, with the Frobenius scalars pinned down as $a_q(g)q$ on the line and $a_q(g)$ on the quotient. It refines the companion statement, in which the sign is only known to square to $1$, by identifying it with the $q$-th coefficient of $g$, and it feeds the construction of the $\lambda$-adic Galois representation attached to $g$ together with its behaviour at primes of multiplicative reduction.
